This page documents an experimental postmarketOS port for the Wi-Fi Samsung
Galaxy Tab S6 Lite (2022), model SM-P613. It uses a downstream SM7125 kernel,
not mainline Linux. No official postmarketOS image is available yet.

== Contributors ==
* Viktor Zaritskyi

== Users owning this device ==
{{Device owners}}

== Hardware notes ==

=== Display and touchscreen ===
The BOE TV104WUM panel, DCS backlight and Himax HX83102E SPI touchscreen work.
The panel needs a delay after reset before its initialization sequence.

=== Audio ===
Internal speakers work through the two TAS2562 amplifiers on QUINARY_MI2S.
The wired headset and microphone paths are not working, so audio is marked
partial. The UCM profile is part of the device package work.

=== Wireless ===
Wi-Fi requires booting the WCN3990 firmware on the modem remote processor.
Bluetooth works, including A2DP, with `ibs_host_sleep=0` for the QCA UART
controller.

== Installation ==
There is no released image or merged device package. This is a developer port;
use the source archive and kernel branch below. Flashing modified boot or
userdata images can erase data or make the device fail to boot. Keep a known
working Android boot image and use Samsung Download Mode for recovery.

== Known limitations ==
* The kernel is downstream and not mainline.
* Wired headset and microphone audio are not working.
* Camera, suspend/resume, sensors, stylus and USB-OTG have not been validated
  for this port.
* Required Qualcomm/Samsung firmware is proprietary and is not distributed in
  the source archive.

